export class LoginPage {

   constructor(private page: Page) {}

   async login(username:string,password:string){
      ...
   }
}

This is the pattern you'll see in mature frameworks at Deloitte, Accenture, Cognizant, Capgemini, and product companies.

For your Deloitte interview

If they ask:

"Why not use only functions and module exports?"

Say:

Functions work well for small utilities, but for page objects I prefer classes because they keep locators and page actions together, improve code organization, support inheritance, and make the framework easier to maintain as it grows.

That's the answer that demonstrates framework design thinking rather than just coding knowledge.